WEBVTT

00:00:09.994 --> 00:00:11.427
Sammy!

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.327
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.427
Go!

00:00:17.161 --> 00:00:19.360
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:19.393 --> 00:00:21.161
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:23.994 --> 00:00:26.293
This is dad's book.

00:00:26.327 --> 00:00:28.161
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off -

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.861
Saving people, hunting
things, the family business.

00:00:31.894 --> 00:00:34.927
I got to find dad. It's the
only think i can think about.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.094
Bethany: now i lay me down to sleep.

00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:44.293
I pray the lord my soul to keep.

00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:47.027
Thy angels watch me through the night

00:00:47.061 --> 00:00:49.794
And keep me safe till morning light.

00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:52.761
Amen.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.260
Night, monkeypuss.

00:01:03.293 --> 00:01:05.094
Daddy?

00:01:05.128 --> 00:01:07.161
Is mommy coming home?

00:01:10.761 --> 00:01:13.027
No, honey.

00:01:13.061 --> 00:01:16.128
She's spending the night at
the hospital with your sister.

00:01:16.161 --> 00:01:17.460
Hey.

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:19.627
You sleep tight now.

00:03:13.977 --> 00:03:17.177
Dean: yeah, you probably
missed something.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.344
Dude, i ran lexisnexis,
local police reports,

00:03:19.377 --> 00:03:21.644
Newspapers
- I couldn't find a single red flag.

00:03:21.677 --> 00:03:23.744
Are you sure you got
the coordinates right?

00:03:23.778 --> 00:03:24.878
Yeah, i double-Checked.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.210
It's fitchburg, wisconsin.

00:03:26.244 --> 00:03:28.210
Dad wouldn't have sent us coordinates

00:03:28.244 --> 00:03:29.878
If it wasn't important, sammy.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.210
Well, i'm telling you, i looked,

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.244
And all i could find was a
big, steamy pile of nothing.

00:03:33.277 --> 00:03:34.577
If dad's sending us
hunting for something,

00:03:34.611 --> 00:03:35.644
I don't know what.

00:03:35.677 --> 00:03:37.144
Well, maybe he's gonna meet us there.

00:03:37.177 --> 00:03:40.344
Yeah, 'cause he's been so
easy to find up to this point.

00:03:40.377 --> 00:03:42.544
You're a real smartass, you know that?

00:03:42.577 --> 00:03:43.910
Don't worry.

00:03:43.943 --> 00:03:46.310
I'm sure there's something
in fitchburg worth killing.

00:03:46.344 --> 00:03:48.544
Yeah? What makes you so sure?

00:03:48.577 --> 00:03:51.744
Because i'm the oldest,
which means i'm always right.

00:03:51.778 --> 00:03:54.477
No, it doesn't. It totally does.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.611
Well, the waitress thinks

00:04:12.644 --> 00:04:15.778
That the local freemasons
are up to something sneaky,

00:04:15.811 --> 00:04:17.077
But other than that,

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.844
Nobody's heard about
anything weird going on.

00:04:19.878 --> 00:04:23.277
Dean, you got the time?

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.577
10 after 4:00.

00:04:25.611 --> 00:04:27.177
Why?

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.344
What's wrong with this picture?

00:04:35.444 --> 00:04:38.677
School's out, isn't it?

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.310
Yeah.

00:04:43.144 --> 00:04:44.811
So where is everybody?

00:04:44.844 --> 00:04:48.577
This place should be
crawling with kids right now.

00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:04.977
It sure is quiet out here.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.778
Yeah, it's a shame.

00:05:06.811 --> 00:05:08.077
Why is that?

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:11.577
You know, kids getting
sick. It's a terrible thing.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.910
How many?

00:05:13.943 --> 00:05:18.444
Just five or six, but
serious, hospital serious.

00:05:18.477 --> 00:05:21.177
A lot of parents are
getting pretty anxious.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.744
They think it's catching.

00:05:36.477 --> 00:05:38.844
Dude, dude, i am not using this i.D.

00:05:38.878 --> 00:05:40.010
Why not?

00:05:40.043 --> 00:05:42.077
Because it says "bikini
inspector" on it.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.043
Don't worry. She won't look that close.

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.844
Hell, she won't even ask to see it.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.210
It's all about confidence, sammy.

00:05:48.344 --> 00:05:50.144
Hi.

00:05:50.177 --> 00:05:53.110
I'm dr. Jerry kaplan,
center for disease control.

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:55.244
Can i see some i.D.?

00:05:58.177 --> 00:06:00.411
Yeah, of course.

00:06:02.744 --> 00:06:05.644
Now, could you direct me
to the pediatrics ward?

00:06:05.677 --> 00:06:09.144
Okay, just go down that hall,
turn left, up the stairs.

00:06:09.177 --> 00:06:10.644
You'll see them.

00:06:10.677 --> 00:06:12.477
Right. Thank you.

00:06:12.511 --> 00:06:14.611
See? Told you it would work.

00:06:14.644 --> 00:06:17.411
Follow me. It's upstairs.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.010
Sam: dean.

00:07:02.344 --> 00:07:04.377
Thanks for seeing us, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:04.411 --> 00:07:06.277
Oh, i'm glad you guys are here.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.677
I was just about to call the cdc myself.

00:07:08.711 --> 00:07:10.444
How did you find out anyway?

00:07:10.477 --> 00:07:12.644
Oh, some g.P. - I
forget his name -

00:07:12.677 --> 00:07:15.677
He called atlanta and must
have beat you to the punch.

00:07:15.711 --> 00:07:18.477
So you say you got six cases so far?

00:07:18.511 --> 00:07:20.878
Yeah, in five weeks.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.411
At first i thought it
was bacterial pneumonia,

00:07:23.444 --> 00:07:24.544
Not that newsworthy.

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.444
But now...

00:07:26.477 --> 00:07:28.611
Now, what?

00:07:28.644 --> 00:07:30.977
The kids aren't
responding to antibiotics.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.277
Their white-Cell
counts keep going down.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.010
Their immune systems just
aren't doing their job.

00:07:36.043 --> 00:07:38.844
It's like their bodies are wearing out.

00:07:38.878 --> 00:07:40.444
Betty: excuse me, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:40.477 --> 00:07:42.244
You ever see anything like this before?

00:07:42.277 --> 00:07:43.411
Never this severe.

00:07:43.444 --> 00:07:45.943
The way it spreads
- That's a new one for me.

00:07:45.977 --> 00:07:47.210
What do you mean?

00:07:47.244 --> 00:07:48.744
It works its way through families,

00:07:48.778 --> 00:07:51.977
But only the children,
one sibling after another.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:55.477
You mind if we interview
a few of the kids?

00:07:55.511 --> 00:07:57.644
They're not conscious.

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.811
None of them?

00:07:59.844 --> 00:08:01.644
No.

00:08:01.677 --> 00:08:04.844
Can we talk to the parents?

00:08:06.277 --> 00:08:08.210
If you think it'll help.

00:08:08.244 --> 00:08:11.811
Yeah, yeah. Who was your
most recent admission?

00:08:11.844 --> 00:08:14.077
I should get back to my girls.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.344
We understand that,

00:08:15.377 --> 00:08:18.077
And we really appreciate
you talking to us.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:20.144
Now, you say mary's the oldest?

00:08:20.177 --> 00:08:21.377
13.

00:08:21.411 --> 00:08:23.577
Okay, and she came down
with it first, right?

00:08:23.611 --> 00:08:24.677
And then...

00:08:24.711 --> 00:08:26.844
Bethany the next night.

00:08:26.878 --> 00:08:28.744
Within 24 hours?

00:08:28.778 --> 00:08:31.511
I guess.

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:34.611
Look, i already went through
all this with the doctor.

00:08:34.644 --> 00:08:36.644
Right. Just a few more
questions, if you don't mind.

00:08:36.677 --> 00:08:38.577
How do you think they caught pneumonia?

00:08:38.611 --> 00:08:40.778
Were they out in the
cold, anything like that?

00:08:40.811 --> 00:08:42.943
No, we think it was an open window.

00:08:42.977 --> 00:08:45.277
Both times?

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.878
The first time, i don't really remember,

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.444
But the second time for sure,

00:08:50.477 --> 00:08:53.477
And i know i closed it
before i put bethany to bed.

00:08:53.511 --> 00:08:55.010
So you think she opened it?

00:08:55.043 --> 00:08:57.577
It's a second-Story window, no ledge.

00:08:57.611 --> 00:08:59.177
No one else could have.

00:09:03.744 --> 00:09:06.310
You know this might not
be anything supernatural.

00:09:06.344 --> 00:09:07.943
It might just be pneumonia.

00:09:07.977 --> 00:09:10.210
Maybe. Or maybe something
opened that window.

00:09:10.244 --> 00:09:13.110
I don't know, man. Look, dad
sent us down here for a reason.

00:09:13.144 --> 00:09:15.444
I think we might be
barking up the right tree.

00:09:15.477 --> 00:09:16.544
I'll tell you one thing.

00:09:16.577 --> 00:09:17.544
What?

00:09:17.577 --> 00:09:19.310
That guy we just talked to -

00:09:19.344 --> 00:09:22.110
I'm betting it'll be a
while before he goes home.

00:09:31.744 --> 00:09:34.177
You got anything over there?

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.878
No, nothing.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:39.244
Yeah, me neither.

00:09:49.878 --> 00:09:51.344
Hey, dean.

00:09:51.377 --> 00:09:53.110
Dean: yeah?

00:09:54.611 --> 00:09:59.377
You were right. It's not pneumonia.

00:10:03.144 --> 00:10:05.310
It's rotted.

00:10:09.244 --> 00:10:11.844
What the hell leaves
a handprint like that?

00:10:15.177 --> 00:10:16.910
<i>Man: cheetara.</i>

00:10:16.943 --> 00:10:18.110
<i>Woman: i am sorry to wake you,</i>

00:10:18.144 --> 00:10:19.544
<i>But jaga bids me to bring you to him.</i>

00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:21.577
John: all right.

00:10:22.611 --> 00:10:24.177
You know the drill, dean.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:26.511
If anyone calls, you don't pick up.

00:10:26.544 --> 00:10:29.878
If it's me, i'll ring
once and then call back.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.244
You got that?

00:10:31.277 --> 00:10:34.577
Mm-Hmm. Don't answer the phone
unless it rings once first.

00:10:34.611 --> 00:10:37.210
Come on, dude. Look alive.
This stuff's important.

00:10:37.244 --> 00:10:38.344
I know, it's just,

00:10:38.377 --> 00:10:40.811
We've done it like a million times,

00:10:40.844 --> 00:10:42.644
And you know i'm not stupid.

00:10:42.677 --> 00:10:44.811
I know you're not, but
it only takes one mistake.

00:10:44.844 --> 00:10:46.210
You got that?

00:10:46.244 --> 00:10:49.611
<i>It's important that he join
jaga on the flight deck.</i>

00:10:49.644 --> 00:10:52.210
All right, if i'm not
back sunday night...

00:10:52.244 --> 00:10:53.611
Call pastor jim.

00:10:55.943 --> 00:10:58.511
Lock the doors and
windows, close the shades,

00:10:58.544 --> 00:10:59.744
And most important -

00:10:59.778 --> 00:11:01.310
Watch out for sammy.

00:11:01.344 --> 00:11:03.677
<i>Responsible for lion-O's
welfare, snarf is.</i>

00:11:03.711 --> 00:11:04.943
I know.

00:11:04.977 --> 00:11:06.611
All right, if something
tries to bust in...

00:11:06.644 --> 00:11:09.611
Shoot first, ask questions later.

00:11:09.644 --> 00:11:11.744
That's my man.

00:11:15.711 --> 00:11:17.010
<i>What's up, jaga?</i>

00:11:17.043 --> 00:11:18.110
<i>Come closer.</i>

00:11:22.943 --> 00:11:25.611
<i>What's happening to her?</i>

00:11:27.544 --> 00:11:29.411
<i>What was that?</i>

00:11:29.444 --> 00:11:32.010
Dean: i know why dad sent us here.

00:11:36.744 --> 00:11:38.844
He's faced this thing before.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:44.778
He wants us to finish the job.

00:12:07.183 --> 00:12:08.884
So what the hell is a shtriga?

00:12:08.917 --> 00:12:10.817
It's kind of like a witch, i think.

00:12:10.851 --> 00:12:12.484
I don't know much about them.

00:12:12.517 --> 00:12:14.484
Well, i've never heard of it,

00:12:14.517 --> 00:12:16.517
And it's not in dad's journal.

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.183
Dad hunted one in fort
douglas, wisconsin,

00:12:19.217 --> 00:12:20.651
About 16, 17 years ago.

00:12:20.684 --> 00:12:23.517
You were there. You don't remember? No.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:26.018
I guess he caught wind that
the thing's in fitchburg now

00:12:26.051 --> 00:12:27.517
And kicked us the coordinates.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:29.784
So wait, this... shtriga.

00:12:29.817 --> 00:12:31.751
Right, you think it's the
same one dad hunted before?

00:12:31.784 --> 00:12:34.283
Yeah, maybe.

00:12:34.317 --> 00:12:36.317
If dad went after it, why
is it still breathing air?

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:37.484
Because it got away.

00:12:37.517 --> 00:12:38.617
Got away?

00:12:38.651 --> 00:12:40.018
Yeah, sammy, it happens.

00:12:40.051 --> 00:12:41.217
Not very often.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.517
I don't know what to tell you.

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:44.384
Maybe dad didn't have
his wheaties that morning.

00:12:44.417 --> 00:12:46.217
What else do you remember?

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.450
Nothing. I was a kid, all right?

00:12:58.217 --> 00:12:59.851
King or two queens?

00:12:59.884 --> 00:13:01.450
Two queens.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.118
Yeah, i bet.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:08.317
What'd you say?

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.283
Nice car.

00:13:10.317 --> 00:13:12.450
Hi. Checking in?

00:13:12.484 --> 00:13:13.684
Yeah.

00:13:13.717 --> 00:13:17.250
Uh, do me a favor. Go get
your brother some dinner.

00:13:17.283 --> 00:13:19.051
I'm helping a guest.

00:13:22.684 --> 00:13:24.851
Two queens.

00:13:26.984 --> 00:13:28.283
Funny kid.

00:13:28.317 --> 00:13:30.150
Oh, yeah, he thinks so.

00:13:30.183 --> 00:13:31.917
Will that be cash or credit?

00:13:31.951 --> 00:13:33.550
Do you take mastercard? Mm-Hmm.

00:13:33.584 --> 00:13:34.584
Perfect.

00:13:34.617 --> 00:13:35.684
There you go.

00:13:35.717 --> 00:13:38.118
Thank you.

00:13:53.984 --> 00:13:56.584
When's dad gonna get back?

00:13:56.617 --> 00:13:58.118
Tomorrow.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.350
When?

00:13:59.384 --> 00:14:00.384
I don't know.

00:14:00.417 --> 00:14:02.250
He usually comes in late, though.

00:14:02.283 --> 00:14:04.018
Now, eat your dinner.

00:14:04.051 --> 00:14:06.283
I'm sick of "scabetti-Os."

00:14:06.317 --> 00:14:08.917
Well, you're the one who wanted them.

00:14:08.951 --> 00:14:10.350
I want lucky charms.

00:14:10.384 --> 00:14:11.951
There's no more lucky charms.

00:14:11.984 --> 00:14:13.250
I saw the box.

00:14:13.283 --> 00:14:14.550
Okay, maybe there is,

00:14:14.584 --> 00:14:17.150
But there's only enough
left for one bowl,

00:14:17.183 --> 00:14:18.751
And i haven't had any yet.

00:14:42.517 --> 00:14:44.951
Do you want the prize?

00:14:44.984 --> 00:14:47.384
Sir?

00:14:49.183 --> 00:14:51.217
Thanks.

00:15:01.851 --> 00:15:03.517
Well, you were right.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:07.283
It wasn't very easy to
find, but you were right.

00:15:07.317 --> 00:15:09.784
A shtriga is a kind of witch.

00:15:09.817 --> 00:15:11.051
They're albanian,

00:15:11.084 --> 00:15:14.018
But legends about them
date back to ancient rome.

00:15:14.051 --> 00:15:16.118
They feed off of spiritus vitae.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.784
Spirit what?

00:15:17.817 --> 00:15:19.084
Vitae. It's latin.

00:15:19.118 --> 00:15:21.183
It translates to "breath of life,"

00:15:21.217 --> 00:15:24.517
Kind of like your life force or essence.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.517
Didn't the doctor say the
kids' bodies were wearing out?

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.484
It's a thought.

00:15:28.517 --> 00:15:29.951
You know, she takes your vitality,

00:15:29.984 --> 00:15:32.118
Maybe your immunity goes to
hell, pneumonia takes hold.

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:35.350
Anyway, shtrigas can feed
off anyone, but they prefer -

00:15:35.384 --> 00:15:37.118
Children.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:38.384
Yeah.

00:15:38.417 --> 00:15:40.484
Probably because they
have stronger life force.

00:15:40.517 --> 00:15:44.118
And get this
- Shtrigas are invulnerable

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.717
To all weapons devised by god and man.

00:15:46.751 --> 00:15:48.951
No, that's not right.

00:15:48.984 --> 00:15:52.450
She's vulnerable when she feeds.

00:15:52.484 --> 00:15:53.484
What?

00:15:53.517 --> 00:15:55.450
If you catch her when she's eating,

00:15:55.484 --> 00:15:58.018
You can blast her with
consecrated wrought irons,

00:15:58.051 --> 00:15:59.884
Buckshots or rounds i think.

00:15:59.917 --> 00:16:01.550
How do you know that?

00:16:01.584 --> 00:16:04.384
Dad told me. I remember.

00:16:04.417 --> 00:16:06.817
Oh.

00:16:06.851 --> 00:16:10.884
So, uh, anything else
dad might have mentioned?

00:16:10.917 --> 00:16:13.217
No, that's it.

00:16:15.283 --> 00:16:17.384
What?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.417
Nothing.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.250
Okay, so, assuming we
can kill it when it eats,

00:16:25.283 --> 00:16:27.084
We've still got to find the thing first,

00:16:27.118 --> 00:16:28.617
Which ain't gonna be a cakewalk.

00:16:28.651 --> 00:16:31.051
Shtrigas take on a human
disguise when they're not hunting.

00:16:31.084 --> 00:16:32.751
What kind of human disguise?

00:16:32.784 --> 00:16:34.584
Historically, something innocuous.

00:16:34.617 --> 00:16:37.417
It could be anything, but it's
usually a feeble old woman,

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.450
Which may be how the witches-As-
Old-Crones legend got started.

00:16:40.484 --> 00:16:41.550
Hang on.

00:16:41.584 --> 00:16:42.651
What?

00:16:44.651 --> 00:16:45.884
Check this out.

00:16:45.917 --> 00:16:48.084
I marked down all the
addresses of the victims.

00:16:48.118 --> 00:16:50.118
Now, these are the houses
that have been hit so far,

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.350
And dead center -

00:16:51.384 --> 00:16:53.584
The hospital.

00:16:53.617 --> 00:16:56.751
When we were there, i saw
a patient, an old woman.

00:16:56.784 --> 00:16:58.183
An old person, huh?

00:16:58.217 --> 00:16:59.250
Yeah.

00:16:59.283 --> 00:17:00.350
In the hospital?

00:17:00.384 --> 00:17:02.417
Whew! Better call the coast guard.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.751
Well, listen, smartass,

00:17:03.784 --> 00:17:06.417
She had an inverted
cross hanging on her wall.

00:17:21.484 --> 00:17:23.651
Betty: good night, dr. Hydaker.

00:17:23.684 --> 00:17:25.217
See you tomorrow, betty.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:27.350
Try to get some sleep, aaron.

00:17:33.384 --> 00:17:34.784
Come on.

00:18:36.183 --> 00:18:38.384
Who the hell are you?

00:18:38.417 --> 00:18:39.684
Who's there?

00:18:41.817 --> 00:18:43.951
You trying to steal my stuff?

00:18:43.984 --> 00:18:45.851
They're always stealing around here.

00:18:45.884 --> 00:18:48.684
No, ma'am, we're
maintenance. We're sorry.

00:18:48.717 --> 00:18:50.317
We thought you were sleeping.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:52.051
Ah, nonsense.

00:18:52.084 --> 00:18:54.384
I was sleeping with my peepers open.

00:18:57.851 --> 00:19:00.817
And fix that crucifix, would you?

00:19:00.851 --> 00:19:04.317
I've asked four damn times already.

00:20:01.707 --> 00:20:05.007
"I was sleeping with my peepers open."

00:20:05.041 --> 00:20:08.341
I almost smoked that old gal, i swear.

00:20:08.374 --> 00:20:09.774
It's not funny.

00:20:10.801 --> 00:20:13.034
Oh, man, you should have
seen your face, dean.

00:20:13.067 --> 00:20:15.667
Oh, yeah, laugh it on, man.
We're back to square one.

00:20:18.234 --> 00:20:20.933
Hang on.

00:20:29.567 --> 00:20:32.200
Hey, what's wrong?

00:20:32.234 --> 00:20:35.134
My brother's sick.

00:20:35.167 --> 00:20:36.301
The little guy?

00:20:36.334 --> 00:20:38.200
Pneumonia.

00:20:38.234 --> 00:20:40.668
He's in the hospital.

00:20:42.067 --> 00:20:43.800
It's my fault.

00:20:43.833 --> 00:20:45.501
No, come on. How?

00:20:46.668 --> 00:20:49.267
I should have made sure
the window was latched.

00:20:49.301 --> 00:20:51.501
He wouldn't have gotten pneumonia

00:20:51.534 --> 00:20:53.167
If the window was latched.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.167
Listen to me.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:03.634
I can promise you that this
is not your fault, okay?

00:21:03.668 --> 00:21:06.100
It's my job to look after him.

00:21:12.933 --> 00:21:14.334
Michael.

00:21:16.768 --> 00:21:19.334
Turn on the "no vacancy"
sign while i'm gone.

00:21:19.367 --> 00:21:21.100
I've got denise covering room service,

00:21:21.134 --> 00:21:22.200
So don't bother with the rooms.

00:21:22.234 --> 00:21:23.567
I'm going with you. Not now, michael.

00:21:23.601 --> 00:21:24.701
But i got to see asher.

00:21:24.734 --> 00:21:26.167
Dean: hey, michael.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.534
Hey.

00:21:27.567 --> 00:21:30.334
I know how you feel.
I'm a big brother, too.

00:21:30.367 --> 00:21:33.067
But you got to go easy on
your mom right now, okay?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:34.267
Aw, damn it.

00:21:34.301 --> 00:21:35.567
I got it.

00:21:35.601 --> 00:21:38.334
Thanks. You're in no condition to drive.

00:21:38.367 --> 00:21:41.100
Why don't you let me give
you a lift to the hospital?

00:21:41.134 --> 00:21:42.434
No, no, i couldn't possibly -

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:46.067
No, no trouble. I insist.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.000
Be good.

00:22:00.668 --> 00:22:02.401
We're gonna kill this thing.

00:22:02.434 --> 00:22:04.501
I want it dead. You hear me?

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:24.134
Dean: hey.

00:22:24.167 --> 00:22:25.567
Hey, how's the kid?

00:22:25.601 --> 00:22:28.034
He's not good. Where you at?

00:22:28.067 --> 00:22:29.601
I'm at the library,

00:22:29.634 --> 00:22:32.167
Trying to find out as much
as i can about this shtriga.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:33.833
Yeah, what do you got?

00:22:33.867 --> 00:22:35.067
Well, bad news.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:37.301
I started with fort douglas

00:22:37.334 --> 00:22:39.501
Around the time you said dad was there.

00:22:39.534 --> 00:22:40.768
And?

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:41.933
Same deal.

00:22:41.967 --> 00:22:45.334
Before that, there was ogdenville.

00:22:45.367 --> 00:22:49.234
Before that, north
haverbrook and brockway.

00:22:49.267 --> 00:22:52.967
Every 15 to 20 years,
it hits a new town.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:56.434
Dean, this thing is just
getting started in fitchburg.

00:22:56.467 --> 00:22:59.367
In all these other places,
it goes on for months,

00:22:59.401 --> 00:23:02.501
Dozens of kids, before the
shtriga finally moves on.

00:23:02.534 --> 00:23:06.100
Kids just languish in
comas, and then they die.

00:23:06.134 --> 00:23:08.301
How far back does this thing go?

00:23:08.334 --> 00:23:09.467
I don't know.

00:23:09.501 --> 00:23:12.167
The earliest mention i
could find is this place

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:14.668
Called black river
falls back in the 1890s.

00:23:14.701 --> 00:23:17.501
Talk about a horror show.

00:23:19.234 --> 00:23:21.501
Whoa.

00:23:21.534 --> 00:23:22.534
Sam?

00:23:22.567 --> 00:23:24.000
Hold on.

00:23:24.034 --> 00:23:26.367
I'm looking at a photograph right now

00:23:26.401 --> 00:23:29.601
Of a bunch of doctors
standing around a kid's bed.

00:23:29.634 --> 00:23:32.501
One of the doctors is hydaker.

00:23:32.534 --> 00:23:34.067
And?

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:37.334
And this picture was taken in 1893.

00:23:37.367 --> 00:23:39.534
You sure?

00:23:39.567 --> 00:23:41.134
Yeah.

00:23:41.167 --> 00:23:43.634
Yeah, absolutely.

00:24:02.134 --> 00:24:06.334
Don't worry. Your son's in good hands.

00:24:06.367 --> 00:24:09.601
I'm gonna take care of him.

00:24:09.634 --> 00:24:12.567
So what's the cdc come up with so far?

00:24:12.601 --> 00:24:15.100
We're still working on a few theories.

00:24:15.134 --> 00:24:17.701
You'll know something as soon as we do.

00:24:17.734 --> 00:24:21.167
Well, nothing's more important
to me than these kids.

00:24:21.200 --> 00:24:22.167
Hmm.

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:24.534
Just let me know if i can help.

00:24:24.567 --> 00:24:27.768
I'll do that.

00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:32.534
Sam: we should have
thought of this before.

00:24:32.567 --> 00:24:35.000
Doctor's a perfect
disguise. You're trusted.

00:24:35.034 --> 00:24:36.900
You can control the whole thing.

00:24:36.933 --> 00:24:40.933
Huh. That son of a bitch.

00:24:40.967 --> 00:24:43.000
I'm surprised you didn't
draw on him right there.

00:24:43.034 --> 00:24:46.000
Yeah, well...

00:24:46.034 --> 00:24:48.000
First of all,

00:24:48.034 --> 00:24:49.967
I'm not gonna open fire in
a freakin' pediatrics ward.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:51.668
Good call.

00:24:51.701 --> 00:24:53.267
Second, it wouldn't have done any good

00:24:53.301 --> 00:24:54.668
Because the bastard's bulletproof

00:24:54.701 --> 00:24:56.267
Unless he's chowing down on something.

00:24:56.301 --> 00:24:57.501
And third, i wasn't packing,

00:24:57.534 --> 00:24:59.067
Which is probably a really good thing

00:24:59.100 --> 00:25:01.200
'Cause i probably would have
just burned a clip in him

00:25:01.234 --> 00:25:02.634
Off of principle alone.

00:25:02.668 --> 00:25:05.234
You're getting wise
in your old age, dean.

00:25:05.267 --> 00:25:06.467
You're damn right.

00:25:06.501 --> 00:25:09.100
'Cause now i know how
we're gonna get it.

00:25:09.134 --> 00:25:11.134
What do you mean?

00:25:11.167 --> 00:25:13.000
The shtriga
- It works through siblings, right?

00:25:13.034 --> 00:25:14.134
Right.

00:25:14.167 --> 00:25:15.534
Well, last night...

00:25:15.567 --> 00:25:16.768
It went after asher.

00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:18.701
Tonight it's probably
gonna come after michael.

00:25:18.734 --> 00:25:19.867
Then we got to get him out of here.

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:22.167
No. No, that would blow the whole deal.

00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:23.668
What? Yeah.

00:25:23.701 --> 00:25:26.100
Then you want to use the kid as bait?

00:25:27.167 --> 00:25:29.933
Are you nuts? No. Forget it.
That's out of the question.

00:25:29.967 --> 00:25:32.467
Sam, it's the only way
- If this thing disappears,

00:25:32.501 --> 00:25:34.800
It could be years before
we get another chance.

00:25:34.833 --> 00:25:36.567
Michael's a kid, and
i'm not gonna dangle him

00:25:36.601 --> 00:25:38.334
In front of that thing
like a worm on a hook.

00:25:38.367 --> 00:25:40.334
Dad did not send me here to walk away.

00:25:40.367 --> 00:25:42.534
<i>Send you here? He didn't send you here.</i>

00:25:42.567 --> 00:25:44.768
<i>He sent us here. This
isn't about you, sam.</i>

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.601
I'm the one that screwed
up. It's my fault.

00:25:46.634 --> 00:25:48.701
There's no telling how
many kids have gotten hurt

00:25:48.734 --> 00:25:49.833
Because of me.

00:25:49.867 --> 00:25:53.434
What are you saying,
dean? How is it your fault?

00:25:59.234 --> 00:26:00.668
Dean.

00:26:00.701 --> 00:26:03.933
You've been hiding
something from the get-Go.

00:26:03.967 --> 00:26:06.601
Since when does dad bail on a hunt?

00:26:06.634 --> 00:26:09.668
Since when does he
let something get away?

00:26:09.701 --> 00:26:14.900
Now, talk to me, man.
Tell me what's going on.

00:26:24.467 --> 00:26:27.234
Fort douglas, wisconsin.

00:26:27.267 --> 00:26:30.267
It was the third night
in this crap room,

00:26:30.301 --> 00:26:32.900
And i was climbing the walls, man.

00:26:32.933 --> 00:26:34.734
I needed to get some air.

00:26:34.768 --> 00:26:36.367
<i>...if ever i saw one.</i>

00:26:36.401 --> 00:26:38.000
<i>Command performance.</i>

00:27:04.933 --> 00:27:06.267
Hey, kid.

00:27:07.434 --> 00:27:09.434
We're closing up.

00:28:12.833 --> 00:28:14.134
Get out of the way!

00:28:24.467 --> 00:28:28.701
Sammy. Sammy. Sammy.

00:28:28.734 --> 00:28:30.000
You okay?

00:28:30.034 --> 00:28:32.768
Sam: dad, what's going on?

00:28:32.800 --> 00:28:34.634
Are you all right?

00:28:38.234 --> 00:28:41.634
What happened?

00:28:41.668 --> 00:28:43.701
I
- I just went out.

00:28:43.734 --> 00:28:45.401
What?

00:28:45.434 --> 00:28:48.067
J
- Just for a second. I'm sorry.

00:28:48.100 --> 00:28:50.467
I told you not to leave this room.

00:28:50.501 --> 00:28:53.467
I told you not to let
him out of your sight.

00:29:05.668 --> 00:29:09.933
Dad just grabbed us and booked,

00:29:09.967 --> 00:29:15.501
Dropped us off at pastor
jim's about three hours away.

00:29:15.534 --> 00:29:18.301
By the time he got back to fort douglas,

00:29:18.334 --> 00:29:20.200
The shtriga had disappeared.

00:29:20.234 --> 00:29:22.467
It was just gone.

00:29:25.501 --> 00:29:29.668
It never resurfaced until now.

00:29:29.701 --> 00:29:32.668
Dad never spoke about it again.

00:29:32.701 --> 00:29:35.701
I didn't ask.

00:29:35.734 --> 00:29:38.234
But he, uh...

00:29:40.401 --> 00:29:45.501
He looked at me different,
you know, which was worse.

00:29:45.534 --> 00:29:47.000
Not that i blame him.

00:29:47.034 --> 00:29:49.900
He gave me an order,
and i didn't listen,

00:29:49.933 --> 00:29:52.067
And i almost got you killed.

00:29:52.100 --> 00:29:53.501
You were just a kid.

00:29:53.534 --> 00:29:57.501
Don't.

00:29:57.534 --> 00:30:02.034
Dad knew this was
unfinished business for me.

00:30:02.067 --> 00:30:05.267
He sent me here to finish it.

00:30:07.334 --> 00:30:11.134
But using michael
- I don't know, dean.

00:30:11.167 --> 00:30:14.367
I mean, how about one of
us hides under the cover?

00:30:14.401 --> 00:30:17.267
You know, we'll be the bait.

00:30:17.301 --> 00:30:20.267
No, that won't work.

00:30:20.301 --> 00:30:23.301
It's got to get close
enough to feed. It'll see us.

00:30:25.867 --> 00:30:28.367
Believe me, i don't like it,
but it's got to be the kid.

00:30:33.967 --> 00:30:35.933
Michael: you're crazy!

00:30:35.967 --> 00:30:38.567
Just go away or i'm calling the cops.

00:30:38.601 --> 00:30:40.634
Hang on a second. Just listen to me.

00:30:40.668 --> 00:30:43.134
You have to believe me, okay?

00:30:43.167 --> 00:30:44.734
This thing came through the window

00:30:44.768 --> 00:30:45.933
And attacked your brother.

00:30:48.501 --> 00:30:49.567
I've seen it.

00:30:49.601 --> 00:30:51.100
I know what it looks like

00:30:51.134 --> 00:30:53.601
'Cause it attacked my brother once, too.

00:31:00.833 --> 00:31:02.768
This thing -

00:31:02.800 --> 00:31:05.434
Is it, like...

00:31:05.467 --> 00:31:10.000
It has this long, black robe?

00:31:10.034 --> 00:31:12.267
You saw it last night, didn't you?

00:31:12.301 --> 00:31:16.267
I thought i was having a nightmare.

00:31:18.334 --> 00:31:22.301
I'd give anything not to tell you this,

00:31:22.334 --> 00:31:24.401
But sometimes nightmares are real.

00:31:24.434 --> 00:31:27.534
<i>So why are you telling me?</i>

00:31:27.567 --> 00:31:29.334
Because we need your help.

00:31:29.367 --> 00:31:30.734
My help?

00:31:30.768 --> 00:31:35.501
We can kill it, me and
him. It's what we do.

00:31:35.534 --> 00:31:37.567
But we can't do it without you.

00:31:37.601 --> 00:31:40.800
What? No.

00:31:40.833 --> 00:31:42.534
Michael, listen to me.

00:31:42.567 --> 00:31:44.301
This thing hurt asher,

00:31:44.334 --> 00:31:47.534
And it's gonna keep hurting
kids unless we stop it.

00:31:47.567 --> 00:31:49.000
Do you understand me?

00:31:51.701 --> 00:31:54.634
Well, that went crappy. Now what?

00:31:54.668 --> 00:31:55.833
What did you expect?

00:31:55.867 --> 00:31:58.434
You can't ask an adult
to do something like that,

00:31:58.467 --> 00:32:00.167
Much less a kid.

00:32:08.401 --> 00:32:11.234
If you kill it, will asher get better?

00:32:16.034 --> 00:32:19.567
Honestly, we don't know.

00:32:22.601 --> 00:32:25.501
You said you're a big brother.

00:32:25.534 --> 00:32:27.734
Yeah.

00:32:27.768 --> 00:32:29.601
You'd take care of your little brother?

00:32:29.634 --> 00:32:33.467
You'd do anything for him?

00:32:33.501 --> 00:32:35.734
Yeah, i would.

00:32:37.634 --> 00:32:41.434
Me too.

00:32:41.467 --> 00:32:42.833
I'll help.

00:33:03.970 --> 00:33:05.604
This camera has night vision on it,

00:33:05.638 --> 00:33:07.638
So we'll be able to
see you as clear as day.

00:33:07.670 --> 00:33:08.870
Are we good?

00:33:08.904 --> 00:33:10.037
Hair to the right.

00:33:10.070 --> 00:33:11.970
There, there.

00:33:12.004 --> 00:33:15.271
Michael: what do i do?

00:33:15.304 --> 00:33:18.904
Just stay under the covers.

00:33:18.937 --> 00:33:22.437
And if it shows up?

00:33:22.471 --> 00:33:24.337
Well, we'll be right in the next room.

00:33:24.371 --> 00:33:26.937
We're gonna come in with
guns, so as soon as we do,

00:33:26.970 --> 00:33:29.304
You roll off this bed
and you crawl under it.

00:33:31.371 --> 00:33:33.104
What if you shoot me?

00:33:33.137 --> 00:33:35.703
We won't shoot you. We're good shots.

00:33:37.337 --> 00:33:40.571
We're not gonna fire
until you're clear, okay?

00:33:40.604 --> 00:33:43.070
Have you heard a gunshot before?

00:33:43.104 --> 00:33:44.737
Like in the movies?

00:33:44.770 --> 00:33:48.337
It's gonna be a lot
louder than in the movies.

00:33:48.371 --> 00:33:51.970
So i want you to stay under
the bed, cover your ears,

00:33:52.004 --> 00:33:55.237
And do not come out until
we say so, you understand?

00:33:58.004 --> 00:34:00.837
Michael, are you sure
you want to do this?

00:34:00.870 --> 00:34:02.604
You don't have to. It's
okay. I won't be mad.

00:34:02.638 --> 00:34:04.638
No, i'm okay.

00:34:04.670 --> 00:34:07.471
Just don't shoot me.

00:34:07.504 --> 00:34:10.737
We're not gonna let
anything happen to you.

00:34:10.770 --> 00:34:12.070
I promise.

00:34:24.870 --> 00:34:26.237
What time is it?

00:34:28.337 --> 00:34:29.504
3:00.

00:34:31.538 --> 00:34:33.371
You sure these iron
rounds are gonna work?

00:34:35.337 --> 00:34:36.770
Consecrated iron rounds.

00:34:36.803 --> 00:34:40.437
And yeah, it's what dad used last time.

00:34:40.471 --> 00:34:43.171
Hey, dean, i'm sorry.

00:34:46.004 --> 00:34:47.070
For what?

00:34:49.703 --> 00:34:51.604
You know...

00:34:51.638 --> 00:34:54.737
I've really given you a lot of crap

00:34:54.770 --> 00:34:58.304
For always following dad's orders,

00:34:58.337 --> 00:35:01.803
But i know why you do it.

00:35:01.837 --> 00:35:03.837
Oh, god. Kill me now.

00:35:09.104 --> 00:35:10.171
Wait, look.

00:35:44.970 --> 00:35:46.604
Now? Not yet.

00:36:21.070 --> 00:36:22.604
Michael, down!

00:36:32.770 --> 00:36:34.471
Mike, you all right? Yeah.

00:36:34.504 --> 00:36:37.204
Just sit tight.

00:36:59.670 --> 00:37:00.703
Dean!

00:37:31.137 --> 00:37:33.037
Dean: hey!

00:37:36.137 --> 00:37:37.937
You okay, little brother?

00:38:10.504 --> 00:38:12.437
It's okay, michael. You can come on out.

00:38:44.977 --> 00:38:47.044
Hey, joanna, how's asher doing?

00:38:47.077 --> 00:38:49.111
Have you seen michael?
Michael: mom! Mom!

00:38:49.144 --> 00:38:50.744
Hey!

00:38:52.244 --> 00:38:53.443
How's ash?

00:38:53.477 --> 00:38:55.577
I've got some good news.
Your brother's gonna be fine.

00:38:55.610 --> 00:38:56.777
Really?

00:38:56.810 --> 00:38:58.777
Yeah, really. No one can explain it.

00:38:58.810 --> 00:39:01.644
It's, uh, it's a miracle.

00:39:01.677 --> 00:39:03.810
They're gonna keep him in
overnight for observation,

00:39:03.844 --> 00:39:05.311
But after that, he's coming home.

00:39:05.344 --> 00:39:06.378
That's great.

00:39:06.410 --> 00:39:08.911
How are all the other kids doing?

00:39:08.944 --> 00:39:10.144
Good, real good.

00:39:10.177 --> 00:39:12.244
A bunch of them should be
checking out in a few days.

00:39:12.278 --> 00:39:14.777
Dr. Travis says the ward's
gonna be like a ghost town.

00:39:14.810 --> 00:39:18.044
Dr. Travis? What about dr. Hydaker?

00:39:18.077 --> 00:39:19.144
Oh, he wasn't in today.

00:39:19.177 --> 00:39:20.877
He must have been sick or something.

00:39:20.911 --> 00:39:23.443
Yeah, yeah, must have.

00:39:23.477 --> 00:39:27.610
So did anything happen while i was gone?

00:39:27.644 --> 00:39:29.610
No, same old stuff.

00:39:29.644 --> 00:39:31.410
Okay. You can go see ash.

00:39:31.443 --> 00:39:32.944
Now? Only if you want to.

00:39:37.543 --> 00:39:38.810
I better get going

00:39:38.844 --> 00:39:41.077
Before he hot-Wires the
car and drives himself.

00:39:47.610 --> 00:39:51.311
It's too bad.

00:39:51.344 --> 00:39:53.944
No, they'll be fine.

00:39:53.977 --> 00:39:55.344
